# Development Flow & Code Review Gate

This rule is the PR/code review checklist. When reviewing code changes or preparing a pull request, verify all items below.

## Pre-PR Checklist (Developer)
1. All artifacts and use cases from sprint planning have been reviewed
2. RAML specification created/updated (if REST API)
3. Implementation meets the RAML specification
4. Code tested locally and working as expected
5. Secure properties configured via secure vault (e.g., Azure Key Vault) for all environments; or if using AES encryption, encryption requested for QA/UAT/Prod
6. MUnit tests included with **at least 70% code coverage**
7. Code pushed to a feature or bugfix branch (not directly to develop)

## Code Review Gate (Reviewer)
The PR **must not be merged** without review and approval. Verify:

### Naming & Structure
- [ ] Project name follows `{name}-{layer}-api` pattern (no regional prefix — deprecated)
- [ ] Flow files are lower-case-hyphenated
- [ ] Flows suffixed with `-flow`, sub-flows with `-sub-flow`, main flow is `{api-spec}-main`
- [ ] No default Studio names on processors or scopes
- [ ] Global config elements are in the global config file only
- [ ] DataWeave scripts are externalized to `src/main/resources/dwls/`
- [ ] Properties files follow `config-{env}.properties` naming

### Quality
- [ ] MUnit tests cover at least 70% of code
- [ ] At least one positive and one negative test per endpoint
- [ ] All external calls are mocked in tests
- [ ] `mvn clean test` passes
- [ ] Postman collection updated for new/modified endpoints

### Security
- [ ] No clear-text secrets in any file
- [ ] Sensitive properties fetched from secure vault (e.g., Azure Key Vault) — or, if AES-encrypted, declared in `mule-artifact.json` `secureProperties`
- [ ] Encryption keys not in source-controlled files

### Documentation
- [ ] `README.md` updated with: project description, business functionality, technical guidelines, release notes
- [ ] Anypoint Exchange home page updated (if published)

### Deployment
- [ ] Version follows semantic versioning (major.minor.patch)
- [ ] Deployment name within 42-character limit
- [ ] Application configured for correct CloudHub private space

### Logging (Insulet Custom Logger Connector)
- [ ] All loggers use `module-logger` — no built-in Mule `logger` component
- [ ] No `category` is mismatched with its operation (Major). Absent `category` is acceptable — connector auto-sets the correct default (Minor: recommend explicit)
- [ ] INFO-level logs use only "Without Payload" operations (category `com.insulet.general`)
- [ ] DEBUG-level logs use only masked or encrypted operations — never raw payload
- [ ] No `tracepoint` is incorrect for its context (Major). Absent `tracepoint` defaults to `FLOW_START` — flag only when context requires a different value (e.g., error handlers need explicit `EXCEPTION`, exit loggers need explicit `FLOW_END`)
- [ ] `sourceSystem` and `targetSystem` set on every logger
- [ ] Error handlers have both INFO (context) and DEBUG (protected payload) entries
- [ ] `log4j2.xml` declares all three `AsyncLogger` categories with correct levels per environment
- [ ] PROD `log4j2.xml` has all categories at WARN (no leftover DEBUG)
- [ ] `sensitiveKeyParts` configured in global connector config
- [ ] `encryptionKey` sourced from secure vault, not hardcoded
